##gff-version 3
##sequence-region NC_001616.1 1 9704
# Potato virus Y (PVY), RefSeq NC_001616.1, 9,704 nt linear +ssRNA
# (genus Potyvirus). The polyprotein example: one CDS whose ten mature
# proteins are given as mature_protein_region_of_CDS rows (GenBank
# mat_peptide), exactly as RefSeq writes them. VirPlot draws them as one box
# split by thin lines, each segment labelled and coloured on its own, as in
# ICTV 9th Report Potyviridae Fig. 2 (which uses TEV; the organisation is the
# same). Coordinates are RefSeq's. Curation:
#  - product= on each mature protein shortened to the figure's label
#    (P1-Pro, HC-Pro, P3, 6K1, CI, 6K2, VPg, NIa-Pro, NIb, CP); RefSeq's
#    "P1 protein", "coat protein" etc. kept in Note=.
#  - PIPO (RefSeq cds-YP_006393460.1, a partial CDS in the +2 frame within P3)
#    given Note=+2 frameshift so VirPlot flips it and writes "+2 FS", as the
#    figure's "PIPO (+2 fs)". It is really reached by polymerase slippage
#    (P3N-PIPO); the figure's wording is kept.
#  - RefSeq's gene rows and polyA_site are omitted (not read by VirPlot).
# Colours in examples/pvy.yml were sampled from the figure. The figure draws
# the polyprotein on the line and PIPO above it; VirPlot's one-strand rule
# puts the polyprotein above and flips PIPO below (conventions doc section 7).
NC_001616.1	RefSeq	region	1	9704	.	+	.	ID=NC_001616.1;Name=PVY;Is_circular=false
NC_001616.1	RefSeq	CDS	185	9376	.	+	0	ID=cds-NP_056759.1;product=polyprotein;protein_id=NP_056759.1
